  "notes": "USAGE:\n{降参|こうさん} can express both literal surrender (in battle, competition) and figurative giving up (to heat, difficulty, a persistent person). In casual speech, もう{降参|こうさん}だ！ is a common way to express that one has had enough.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {降参|こうさん}する (to surrender, to give in)\n- もう{降参|こうさん}だ (I give up already)\n- {降参|こうさん}させる (to make someone give in)\n- {暑|あつ}さに{降参|こうさん}する (to be defeated by the heat)",
